---
description: Core conventions for every change in the Flows repo
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read `AGENTS.md` first. It holds the current app state and commands.
- KISS and YAGNI: build what the current step needs. No speculative
  abstractions, options or packages.
- Use pnpm only (see `packageManager` in `package.json`). Add deps with
  `pnpm --filter <pkg> add <dep>`; quote version specifiers in zsh.
- TypeScript strict, ESM. Validate external input with zod. Shared types
  live in `packages/shared`.
- Local only: bind every server to `127.0.0.1`, never `0.0.0.0`.
- Before calling work done, run `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`,
  and `pnpm test:e2e` for UI or API changes. Report the results.
- When you add, remove or rename a package, command, route or feature,
  update the "App state" section of `AGENTS.md`. Keep `AGENTS.md` at 150
  lines or fewer; trim old detail rather than exceed it.
- Branch from `develop`, target PRs at `develop`. Commit in small,
  verified steps with conventional messages. Never push or merge to
  `main` without explicit approval for that change.
- No person's name in code, docs or metadata. Never commit secrets or
  `.env` files.
